  "summary": "This festive <b>Moroccan lamb stew</b> is crafted for special gatherings, blending tender cuts of shoulder with warm aromatic spices and sweet dried fruits. Softened red onions form a gentle aromatic base, while a handcrafted blend of ras el hanout infuses the pot with warm notes of cardamom, cumin, nutmeg, and ginger. Premium saffron threads steeped directly in broth release a brilliant golden hue and floral perfume throughout the bubbling liquid. Sweet dried figs slowly rehydrate in the cooking vessel, absorbing the savory lamb juices while imparting a natural fruit honey sweetness that balances the earthy spices. Slowly simmering inside a traditional tagine yields remarkably succulent meat that yields effortlessly to a fork. A final drizzle of golden honey pulled into the reducing sauce creates a glistening glaze over each piece of lamb. Topped with crunchy toasted almonds and bright cilantro leaves, this regal dish provides a breathtaking centerpiece for celebratory feasts, best served over fluffly steamed couscous or with fresh flatbread.",
